, "uuid": "1ATC9Olj8d", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 15, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8764923, "raw_content": "How dumb can people be?  This would have been a huge boom to their economy.", "author": "FartOnLibtards", "created": 1785942475293, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Cakes4077", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Missouri rejects No Income Tax?  WTF", "last_comment_created": 1785948325480, "content": "<p>How dumb can people be?  This would have been a huge boom to their economy.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 15, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATC9OlAuH", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 25, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "fight", "id": 8764701, "raw_content": "", "author": "mateus", "created": 1785932343081, "profile_picture": "jDN5h0vfxmz2", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.ncronline.org", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATC9OlAuH.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.ncronline.org/news/court-shields-women-religious-ny-assisted-suicide-law", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Court \"temporarily shields\"  four orders of Catholic nuns from NY's new assisted suicide law until their lawsuit is heard. The state is forcing them to provide info regarding the law and implement related policies in their end-of-life care facilities. ", "last_comment_created": 1785932343081, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 25, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "The groups sued the state July 17, arguing the law would require them to facilitate such deaths for their patients in violation of their faith.", "large_image": "BeXG3owKwKi4wJni.png", "title": "Court shields women religious from NY assisted suicide law "}, "post_flair_text": "FIGHT,\u00a0\u00a0FIGHT,\u00a0\u00a0FIGHT!", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATC9OlBJ7", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 21, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8764765, "raw_content": "", "author": "MAG-n-KAG", "created": 1785935756483, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "AngelMark2", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATC9OlBJ7.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/CtRDm3FBwCAR.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/MxYgtA0WriFn1UUO.png", "width": 500, "content-type": "png", "height": 569}], "blurhash": "UJLW#E~W8_kD?GkWMxxuozt7V[Rj-UyER5RP", "full_resolution": [569, 500]}, "title": "\"Muh two weeks\" for thee, not for me", "last_comment_created": 1785941387635, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 15, "score_up": 21, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATC9OlRxM", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 19, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8764804, "raw_content": "There has always been election fraud but it's much easier and more wide spread now.\n\nFurther, there is no AIR GAP in election equip.  To understand this it is necessary to understand what AIR GAP means.\n\nIn plumbing an air gap is required for certain devices, such as a commercial ice maker.  Some call this an indirect drain.  A drain line is required to be suspended above the drain device in a manner that would allow the drain device to overflow and not reach the ice maker drain.  i.e.  Has to be physical space adequate that overflowing dirty water could not come in contact with the drain from the ice maker.  \n\nThe plumbing example makes it very clear what the purpose of an air gap is.\n\nIn the digital world, simply having a LAN cable disconnected from a device is not an air gap, because it can be reconnected quite easily.  Further most devices have an 802.ll bgn chip which allows wireless connection.  What about a usb stick?  Still no air gap as a stick can be easily inserted.  To truly air gap election machinery there would have to be complete independence of the device w/ programming being limited to something like an rs-232 serial interface only, which requires more effort to connect and will not interconnect with other devices.\n\nWe have learned from 2020 that all of these devices were networked or networkable.  NO AIR GAP.\n\nMail ballots?  Quite easy the flood the zone, get an initial count, then dispatch the court brigades to preserve it.  Push the idea, better to allow 1000 fraudulent votes that take a chance on throwing out a single legitimate vote.  When you get right down to it, that is their marketing pitch.  \n\nThese are flawed systems and that is not the byproduct of a large number of voters.  It is rather a design feature to control the outcome.", "author": "dataonly", "created": 1785937681612, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "ErikaLives", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Election Fraud is Not an Unintended Consequence - It's a FEATURE!", "last_comment_created": 1785937759895, "content": "<p>There has always been election fraud but it's much easier and more wide spread now.</p>\n<p>Further, there is no AIR GAP in election equip.  To understand this it is necessary to understand what AIR GAP means.</p>\n<p>In plumbing an air gap is required for certain devices, such as a commercial ice maker.  Some call this an indirect drain.  A drain line is required to be suspended above the drain device in a manner that would allow the drain device to overflow and not reach the ice maker drain.  i.e.  Has to be physical space adequate that overflowing dirty water could not come in contact with the drain from the ice maker.</p>\n<p>The plumbing example makes it very clear what the purpose of an air gap is.</p>\n<p>In the digital world, simply having a LAN cable disconnected from a device is not an air gap, because it can be reconnected quite easily.  Further most devices have an 802.ll bgn chip which allows wireless connection.  What about a usb stick?  Still no air gap as a stick can be easily inserted.  To truly air gap election machinery there would have to be complete independence of the device w/ programming being limited to something like an rs-232 serial interface only, which requires more effort to connect and will not interconnect with other devices.</p>\n<p>We have learned from 2020 that all of these devices were networked or networkable.  NO AIR GAP.</p>\n<p>Mail ballots?  Quite easy the flood the zone, get an initial count, then dispatch the court brigades to preserve it.  Push the idea, better to allow 1000 fraudulent votes that take a chance on throwing out a single legitimate vote.  When you get right down to it, that is their marketing pitch.</p>\n<p>These are flawed systems and that is not the byproduct of a large number of voters.  It is rather a design feature to control the outcome.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 19, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATC9OktrE", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 35, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8764600, "raw_content": "", "author": "rdvs34283", "created": 1785925693552, "profile_picture": "p9HQtdiLq2uP", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "motrhed3", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "hotair.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATC9OktrE.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://hotair.com/david-strom/2026/08/04/will-the-chickens-come-home-to-roost-for-pravda-n3817644", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "The vice president started raising chickens, so the Washington Post called the city of DC on him and tried to get him cited for a zoning infraction